export const CONCIERGE_INTEGRATION_KNOWLEDGE = "# ChainMore Integration Knowledge\n\nSurface: signed-in merchants only.\n\nThe Concierge gets this file only when the dashboard server has proven that\nthe visitor is signed in. Everything here is also in the public docs at\n`chainmore.io/docs.html` and `chainmore.io/errors`; this file adds working\ncode and the answers to common mistakes. Never guess an address, header,\nfield, event name or error code that is not written here.\n\n## Addresses\n\n- API: `https://api.chainmore.io`\n- Checkout page for the customer: `https://checkout.chainmore.io`\n- Merchant dashboard: `https://app.chainmore.io`\n- Public docs: `https://chainmore.io/docs.html`, errors: `https://chainmore.io/errors`\n\nThere is no public SDK package. Integrate with plain HTTPS from the\nmerchant's server, in any language.\n\n## The five steps\n\n1. API key: dashboard, API keys, create key. A key starting with `cm_test_`\n   works in test mode, `cm_live_` in live mode. The mode comes from the key;\n   there is no mode parameter. Test and live are kept apart: a link created\n   with a test key is invisible to a live key. The key is shown once and\n   belongs on the merchant's server only, never in a browser or app.\n2. Payout destination: dashboard, Payouts, add the receiving wallet address.\n   Without one, a checkout link offers no payment method.\n3. Create a payment: `POST https://api.chainmore.io/v1/checkout/links` from\n   the merchant's server.\n4. Send the customer to\n   `https://checkout.chainmore.io/checkout/?token=<checkout_token>` as a full\n   page or in a new tab. It does not work inside an iframe. After a\n   successful payment the checkout shows a button back to `return_url`. There\n   is no cancel address and no automatic redirect.\n5. Webhooks: dashboard, Webhooks, add an endpoint. Ship the order only after a\n   signed `payment.settled` or `payment_intent.settled` event.\n\nWhen everything works in test mode, the merchant emails\n`support@chainmore.io`. The team switches the account to live mode; then the\nmerchant creates a `cm_live_` key.\n\n## Creating a checkout link\n\nHeaders:\n\n- `Authorization: Bearer <api key>`\n- `Content-Type: application/json`\n- `Idempotency-Key: <one value per order>`, required on every POST, PUT,\n  PATCH and DELETE.\n\nBody fields:\n\n- `amount_minor` (required): whole number in the currency's smallest unit.\n  `2500` means 25.00.\n- `currency` (required): `USD` or `EUR`. The stablecoin methods `usdt0` and\n  `usdc` need `USD`. `EUR` is only for card payments, and those are only\n  offered where the account has them switched on.\n- `merchant_order_id` (optional, recommended): the merchant's own order\n  number, 1 to 128 characters from letters, digits and `. _ : -`.\n- `return_url` (optional): must start with `https://`. The checkout shows a\n  button back to it after a successful payment.\n- `metadata` (optional): any valid JSON the merchant wants stored with the\n  link.\n\nAnswer: `201 Created` the first time. Fields: `checkout_link_id`,\n`checkout_token` (starts with `cl_`), `state` (`open`), `amount_minor`,\n`currency`, `merchant_order_id`, `available_payment_methods`, `created_at`,\n`expires_at`. A link stays open for 24 hours.\n\nThe same request again with the same `Idempotency-Key` answers `200` with the\nsame link but without `checkout_token`. Save the first checkout URL securely\nwith its order and `checkout_link_id` before redirecting the customer. On a\nrepeat, reuse that saved URL only for the same order and link. If the first\nanswer or URL was lost and no saved URL exists, stop this checkout attempt.\nRead the existing link's status and contact `support@chainmore.io` with the\norder ID, `checkout_link_id` and `correlation_id` when available, never the\nkey, token or URL. Do not create a new link, payment or `Idempotency-Key` to\nrecover a missing token: that can create another independently payable link.\nThere is no token recovery API documented here. The same `Idempotency-Key`\nwith a different body is\nrefused with `400 invalid_request` and the detail\n\"checkout link idempotency key reused with different facts\".\n\n`available_payment_methods` lists only what this account can take for this\nlink: `usdt0` (USDT), `usdc` (USDC) and `card`. Do not promise a method that\nis not in the list.\n\ncurl:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.chainmore.io/v1/checkout/links \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $CHAINMORE_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Idempotency-Key: order-1042\" \\\n  -d '{\"amount_minor\": 2500, \"currency\": \"USD\", \"merchant_order_id\": \"order-1042\", \"return_url\": \"https://shop.example/thanks\"}'\n```\n\nThe examples below use the merchant's own durable order storage.\n`saveCheckout` / `save_checkout` must save the record with that order before\nreturning; if saving fails, do not redirect. Load the saved record only from\nthat same order. Keep checkout URLs server-side and out of logs. None of the\nexamples starts a replacement request when the token is missing.\n\nNode.js 18 or newer (`order.checkoutLink` is that order's saved record):\n\n```js\nasync function createCheckoutLink(order, saveCheckout) {\n  const res = await fetch(\"https://api.chainmore.io/v1/checkout/links\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: {\n      Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.CHAINMORE_API_KEY}`,\n      \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n      \"Idempotency-Key\": `order-${order.id}`,\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify({\n      amount_minor: order.amountMinor,\n      currency: \"USD\",\n      merchant_order_id: `order-${order.id}`,\n      return_url: \"https://shop.example/thanks\",\n    }),\n  });\n  const link = await res.json();\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`ChainMore ${res.status} ${link.code}: ${link.detail} (correlation_id ${link.correlation_id})`);\n  }\n  if (typeof link.checkout_link_id !== \"string\" || !link.checkout_link_id) {\n    throw new Error(\"ChainMore response has no checkout_link_id; stop and check the existing order.\");\n  }\n  if (typeof link.checkout_token !== \"string\" || !link.checkout_token) {\n    const saved = order.checkoutLink;\n    if (saved?.merchant_order_id === `order-${order.id}` &&\n        saved.checkout_link_id === link.checkout_link_id &&\n        typeof saved.url === \"string\" && saved.url) return saved.url;\n    throw new Error(\"Checkout token unavailable; stop, check the existing link status and contact support with its ID. Do not create a replacement link.\");\n  }\n  const url = `https://checkout.chainmore.io/checkout/?token=${encodeURIComponent(link.checkout_token)}`;\n  await saveCheckout(order.id, { merchant_order_id: `order-${order.id}`, checkout_link_id: link.checkout_link_id, url });\n  return url;\n}\n```\n\nPython with `requests`:\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\nimport requests\n\ndef create_checkout_link(order_id: str, amount_minor: int, save_checkout, saved_checkout=None) -> str:\n    resp = requests.post(\n        \"https://api.chainmore.io/v1/checkout/links\",\n        headers={\n            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['CHAINMORE_API_KEY']}\",\n            \"Idempotency-Key\": f\"order-{order_id}\",\n        },\n        json={\n            \"amount_minor\": amount_minor,\n            \"currency\": \"USD\",\n            \"merchant_order_id\": f\"order-{order_id}\",\n            \"return_url\": \"https://shop.example/thanks\",\n        },\n        timeout=15,\n    )\n    link = resp.json()\n    if not resp.ok:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"ChainMore {resp.status_code} {link.get('code')}: {link.get('detail')} (correlation_id {link.get('correlation_id')})\")\n    link_id = link.get(\"checkout_link_id\")\n    if not isinstance(link_id, str) or not link_id:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"ChainMore response has no checkout_link_id; stop and check the existing order.\")\n    token = link.get(\"checkout_token\")\n    if not isinstance(token, str) or not token:\n        saved = saved_checkout or {}\n        if (saved.get(\"merchant_order_id\") == f\"order-{order_id}\" and\n                saved.get(\"checkout_link_id\") == link_id and\n                isinstance(saved.get(\"url\"), str) and saved[\"url\"]):\n            return saved[\"url\"]\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Checkout token unavailable; stop, check the existing link status and contact support with its ID. Do not create a replacement link.\")\n    url = \"https://checkout.chainmore.io/checkout/?token=\" + quote(token, safe=\"\")\n    save_checkout(order_id, {\"merchant_order_id\": f\"order-{order_id}\", \"checkout_link_id\": link_id, \"url\": url})\n    return url\n```\n\nPHP with cURL:\n\n```php\n<?php\nfunction create_checkout_link(string $orderId, int $amountMinor, callable $saveCheckout, ?array $savedCheckout = null): string\n{\n    $ch = curl_init('https://api.chainmore.io/v1/checkout/links');\n    curl_setopt_array($ch, [\n        CURLOPT_POST => true,\n        CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER => true,\n        CURLOPT_TIMEOUT => 15,\n        CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER => [\n            'Authorization: Bearer ' . getenv('CHAINMORE_API_KEY'),\n            'Content-Type: application/json',\n            'Idempotency-Key: order-' . $orderId,\n        ],\n        CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS => json_encode([\n            'amount_minor' => $amountMinor,\n            'currency' => 'USD',\n            'merchant_order_id' => 'order-' . $orderId,\n            'return_url' => 'https://shop.example/thanks',\n        ]),\n    ]);\n    $raw = curl_exec($ch);\n    $status = curl_getinfo($ch, CURLINFO_HTTP_CODE);\n    curl_close($ch);\n    if ($raw === false) {\n        throw new RuntimeException('Checkout response unavailable; retry only the same request with the same Idempotency-Key.');\n    }\n    $link = json_decode($raw, true);\n    if (!is_array($link)) {\n        throw new RuntimeException('Invalid checkout response; stop and check the existing order.');\n    }\n    if ($status < 200 || $status >= 300) {\n        throw new RuntimeException(\"ChainMore {$status} {$link['code']}: {$link['detail']} (correlation_id {$link['correlation_id']})\");\n    }\n    $linkId = $link['checkout_link_id'] ?? null;\n    if (!is_string($linkId) || $linkId === '') {\n        throw new RuntimeException('ChainMore response has no checkout_link_id; stop and check the existing order.');\n    }\n    $token = $link['checkout_token'] ?? null;\n    if (!is_string($token) || $token === '') {\n        if (($savedCheckout['merchant_order_id'] ?? null) === 'order-' . $orderId &&\n            ($savedCheckout['checkout_link_id'] ?? null) === $linkId &&\n            is_string($savedCheckout['url'] ?? null) && $savedCheckout['url'] !== '') {\n            return $savedCheckout['url'];\n        }\n        throw new RuntimeException('Checkout token unavailable; stop, check the existing link status and contact support with its ID. Do not create a replacement link.');\n    }\n    $url = 'https://checkout.chainmore.io/checkout/?token=' . rawurlencode($token);\n    $saveCheckout($orderId, ['merchant_order_id' => 'order-' . $orderId, 'checkout_link_id' => $linkId, 'url' => $url]);\n    return $url;\n}\n```\n\n## Webhooks\n\nSetup: dashboard, Webhooks, add an endpoint. It must be a public `https`\naddress; localhost and private network addresses are refused. The signing\nsecret starts with `whsec_` and is shown once. Each endpoint has its own\nsecret, and test and live are set up separately.\n\nEvery delivery is a `POST` with a JSON body and these headers:\n\n- `X-ChainMore-Timestamp`: send time in RFC 3339 UTC, for example\n  `2026-10-07T08:00:00Z`.\n- `X-ChainMore-Signature`: lowercase hex HMAC-SHA256.\n- `X-ChainMore-Signature-Previous`: only while a secret is being rotated, for\n  14 days, made with the old secret.\n- `X-ChainMore-Event-ID`: the same value as `event_id` in the body.\n\nChecking the signature:\n\n1. Read the raw body exactly as received. Do not parse and re-encode it first.\n2. Signed message: the timestamp header, a dot, then the raw body.\n3. Key: the whole `whsec_…` secret used as text, not decoded.\n4. Compare the hex result with `X-ChainMore-Signature`, and with\n   `X-ChainMore-Signature-Previous` when present, in constant time.\n5. Reject the delivery when the timestamp is more than five minutes away from\n   the server clock.\n\nAnswering: send a 2xx status within 10 seconds. Anything else, 4xx included,\ncounts as failed. ChainMore tries again after 1 second, 5 seconds, 30\nseconds, 5 minutes and 30 minutes. After that the delivery stays failed and\ncan be sent again in the dashboard under Deliveries.\n\nThe same event can arrive more than once. Process each `event_id` once and\nmake \"mark order paid\" safe to run twice, because a resend from the dashboard\ncarries a new `event_id`. Events can arrive in any order. Ignore event types\nyou do not use, but still answer 2xx. New fields can appear in the body;\nignore the ones you do not use.\n\nWhich event to wait for:\n\n- `payment.settled`: USDT and every other method except cross-network USDC.\n- `payment_intent.settled`: USDC that crosses networks.\n- Listen for both. Ship the order only after one of them, and check that the\n  amount and `merchant_order_id` match the order. A customer coming back to\n  the shop, or a transaction hash, does not prove the payment.\n- If the link was created without `merchant_order_id`, the event carries the\n  `checkout_link_id` in that field.\n\nExample `payment.settled` body:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"event_type\": \"payment.settled\",\n  \"event_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n  \"occurred_at\": \"2026-10-07T08:00:00Z\",\n  \"payment_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n  \"merchant_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n  \"merchant_order_id\": \"order-1042\",\n  \"state\": \"settled\",\n  \"amount\": { \"minor\": 2500, \"currency\": \"USD\", \"asset\": \"USDT\" }\n}\n```\n\nExample `payment_intent.settled` body. `usdc_atomic` is a string with six\ndecimals: `25000000` means 25 USDC.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"event_type\": \"payment_intent.settled\",\n  \"event_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n  \"occurred_at\": \"2026-10-07T08:00:00Z\",\n  \"payment_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n  \"merchant_id\": \"<uuid>\",\n  \"mode\": \"test\",\n  \"surface_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"merchant_order_id\": \"order-1042\",\n  \"amount\": { \"usdc_atomic\": \"25000000\", \"asset\": \"USDC\" },\n  \"route\": { \"source_chain\": \"base\", \"dest_chain\": \"arbitrum\", \"finality_mode\": \"fast\" },\n  \"settlement\": { \"source_tx_hash\": \"0x…\", \"mint_tx_hash\": \"0x…\", \"merchant_wallet\": \"0x…\", \"settlement_contract\": \"0x…\" }\n}\n```\n\nTest event: dashboard, Webhooks, the endpoint, \"Send test event\". It sends a\nsigned `payment_intent.settled` (or `payment.settled` when the endpoint only\nlistens to that) with `\"test_event\": true` and made-up ids. Check the\nsignature as usual, answer 2xx, and do not ship anything for it. Test events\ncannot be resent from Deliveries; send a new one instead.\n\nNode.js with Express. The raw body parser matters: `express.json()` would\nchange the bytes before the check.\n\n```js\nimport crypto from \"node:crypto\";\nimport express from \"express\";\n\nconst app = express();\nconst SECRET = process.env.CHAINMORE_WEBHOOK_SECRET; // whsec_…\n\napp.post(\"/chainmore/webhook\", express.raw({ type: \"application/json\" }), async (req, res) => {\n  const timestamp = req.get(\"X-ChainMore-Timestamp\") ?? \"\";\n  const sent = Date.parse(timestamp);\n  if (!Number.isFinite(sent) || Math.abs(Date.now() - sent) > 5 * 60 * 1000) {\n    return res.status(400).send(\"timestamp too old\");\n  }\n\n  const expected = crypto.createHmac(\"sha256\", SECRET).update(`${timestamp}.`).update(req.body).digest(\"hex\");\n  const matches = (sig) => typeof sig === \"string\" && sig.length === expected.length &&\n    crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(sig), Buffer.from(expected));\n  if (!matches(req.get(\"X-ChainMore-Signature\")) && !matches(req.get(\"X-ChainMore-Signature-Previous\"))) {\n    return res.status(400).send(\"bad signature\");\n  }\n\n  const event = JSON.parse(req.body.toString(\"utf8\"));\n  if (event.test_event) return res.sendStatus(200);\n  try {\n    if (event.event_type === \"payment.settled\" || event.event_type === \"payment_intent.settled\") {\n      await markOrderPaid(event.merchant_order_id, event.event_id, event); // your code, safe to run twice\n    }\n    res.sendStatus(200);\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error(err);\n    res.sendStatus(500); // ChainMore tries again\n  }\n});\n```\n\nPython with Flask:\n\n```python\nimport hashlib\nimport hmac\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\nSECRET = os.environ[\"CHAINMORE_WEBHOOK_SECRET\"].encode()  # whsec_…, used as text\n\n@app.post(\"/chainmore/webhook\")\ndef chainmore_webhook():\n    body = request.get_data()  # raw bytes, before any parsing\n    timestamp = request.headers.get(\"X-ChainMore-Timestamp\", \"\")\n    try:\n        sent = datetime.fromisoformat(timestamp.replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\"))\n    except ValueError:\n        return \"bad timestamp\", 400\n    if abs((datetime.now(timezone.utc) - sent).total_seconds()) > 300:\n        return \"timestamp too old\", 400\n\n    expected = hmac.new(SECRET, timestamp.encode() + b\".\" + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    signatures = [request.headers.get(\"X-ChainMore-Signature\", \"\"),\n                  request.headers.get(\"X-ChainMore-Signature-Previous\", \"\")]\n    if not any(sig and hmac.compare_digest(sig, expected) for sig in signatures):\n        return \"bad signature\", 400\n\n    event = json.loads(body)\n    if event.get(\"test_event\"):\n        return \"\", 200\n    if event[\"event_type\"] in (\"payment.settled\", \"payment_intent.settled\"):\n        mark_order_paid(event[\"merchant_order_id\"], event[\"event_id\"], event)  # your code, safe to run twice\n    return \"\", 200\n```\n\nPHP:\n\n```php\n<?php\n$secret = getenv('CHAINMORE_WEBHOOK_SECRET'); // whsec_…, used as text\n$body = file_get_contents('php://input');      // raw body, before any parsing\n$timestamp = $_SERVER['HTTP_X_CHAINMORE_TIMESTAMP'] ?? '';\n$signature = $_SERVER['HTTP_X_CHAINMORE_SIGNATURE'] ?? '';\n$previous = $_SERVER['HTTP_X_CHAINMORE_SIGNATURE_PREVIOUS'] ?? '';\n\n$sent = strtotime($timestamp);\nif ($sent === false || abs(time() - $sent) > 300) {\n    http_response_code(400);\n    exit('timestamp too old');\n}\n\n$expected = hash_hmac('sha256', $timestamp . '.' . $body, $secret);\n$valid = hash_equals($expected, $signature) || ($previous !== '' && hash_equals($expected, $previous));\nif (!$valid) {\n    http_response_code(400);\n    exit('bad signature');\n}\n\n$event = json_decode($body, true);\nif (!empty($event['test_event'])) {\n    http_response_code(200);\n    exit;\n}\nif (in_array($event['event_type'], ['payment.settled', 'payment_intent.settled'], true)) {\n    mark_order_paid($event['merchant_order_id'], $event['event_id'], $event); // your code, safe to run twice\n}\nhttp_response_code(200);\n```\n\nFrameworks that parse JSON before the handler (Next.js route handlers,\nNestJS, Laravel middleware, Django REST framework) need the raw body: in a\nNext.js route handler use `await request.text()` and check that string; in\nLaravel use `$request->getContent()`; in Django use `request.body`.\n\nLocal development: the endpoint must be a public `https` address, so\n`localhost` does not work. Use a tunnel tool that gives a public https\naddress for the local server, register that address as a test endpoint, and\nuse \"Send test event\".\n\n## Checking a status\n\n- `GET /v1/checkout/links/{id}` with the API key. `state` is `open` (waiting\n  for the customer), `bound` (the customer chose a payment method; this does\n  not mean paid) or `expired`. A bound link has `payment_method` and either\n  `payment_id` or `intent_id`.\n- `GET /v1/payments/{payment_id}`: paid when `public_status` is `completed`.\n  `failed` and `expired` mean no money arrived. Anything else is still in\n  progress.\n- `GET /v1/payment-intents/{intent_id}`: paid when `surface_status` is\n  `completed`.\n- Webhooks are the main signal. Use these reads as a backup, for example in a\n  job that checks open orders, not in a tight loop.\n\n## Test mode\n\nUSDT and USDC payments in test mode run on the real networks and move real\nfunds. Use small amounts and a wallet the merchant controls.\n\n## Errors\n\nEvery error is `application/problem+json` with `code`, `title`, `detail`,\n`docs_url` (`chainmore.io/errors/<code>`) and `correlation_id`. Match on\n`code`, not on the text. Ask the merchant for the status, `code`, `detail`\nand `correlation_id`, never for the key.\n\n- `400 idempotency_required`: the `Idempotency-Key` header is missing. Use one\n  value per order and the same value when retrying the same request.\n- `400 invalid_json`: the body is not valid JSON, or `Content-Type` is not\n  `application/json`.\n- `400 invalid_request`: a field is missing, malformed or out of range. The\n  `detail` names it. Typical causes: `amount_minor` as text or with decimals,\n  a currency other than `USD` or `EUR`, a `merchant_order_id` with spaces or\n  other characters, `return_url` without `https://`, or an `Idempotency-Key`\n  reused with a different body.\n- `401 unauthorized`: the key is missing, wrong or revoked, or the header is\n  not exactly `Authorization: Bearer cm_test_…` (or `cm_live_…`).\n- `401 wrong_auth_kind`: the route belongs to the dashboard (API keys, webhook\n  endpoints, dashboard data). Do that step in the dashboard.\n- `404 not_found` or `404 checkout_link_not_found`: wrong id or token, or the\n  object belongs to the other mode (test key against a live object or the\n  other way round).\n- `409 checkout_link_already_bound`: the customer already chose another\n  method on this link. Continue with the payment the link points to.\n- `409 checkout_link_method_unavailable`: the method is not in\n  `available_payment_methods` for this link, often because the currency does\n  not fit (`USD` for USDT and USDC) or no payout destination exists for it.\n- `409 merchant_limit_reached`: the payment is above the account's limits.\n  The merchant contacts `support@chainmore.io`.\n- `410 checkout_link_expired`: the 24 hours passed before the customer chose\n  a method. Create a new link.\n- `429 rate_limited`: too many requests. Wait, honour `Retry-After` when\n  present, and retry with the same `Idempotency-Key`.\n- `503 handouts_paused` or `503 rail_not_ready`: new payment steps are paused\n  for a moment. Retry later. Payments already sent are still completed.\n- Other 5xx: retry with the same `Idempotency-Key`. If it continues, email\n  `support@chainmore.io` with the `correlation_id`.\n\nCommon problems without an error code:\n\n- Empty `available_payment_methods`: usually no payout destination yet. Add\n  one under Payouts. If it stays empty, email `support@chainmore.io`.\n- Checkout page shows 404: the customer was sent to the API host. The\n  checkout lives on `checkout.chainmore.io/checkout/?token=…`.\n- Checkout inside an iframe stays blank: open it as a full page or new tab.\n- Signature never matches: the body was parsed or re-encoded before the\n  check, the secret was decoded instead of used as text, the timestamp and\n  dot are missing from the signed message, the comparison used the wrong\n  case, or the secret belongs to another endpoint or mode.\n- Webhooks do not arrive: the endpoint must be public `https`, answer 2xx\n  within 10 seconds and be enabled and subscribed to the event. Deliveries in\n  the dashboard shows every attempt and the answer the server gave.\n- Order marked paid twice: the handler is not safe to run twice. Store the\n  `event_id`, and make the order update a no-op when the order is already\n  paid.\n- Token missing in the response: the request was a repeat with the same\n  `Idempotency-Key`. Reuse the first URL saved with the same order and link.\n  If none was saved, stop, check the existing link's status and contact\n  support with non-secret IDs. Never create a replacement link or key to\n  recover the token, and never redirect with an empty or undefined token.\n\n## Going live\n\n1. A full test payment works: link created, customer pays, the signed event\n   arrives, the order is marked paid once.\n2. \"Send test event\" passes the signature check, and a repeated delivery does\n   not ship twice.\n3. Keys and the webhook secret live in server environment variables, not in\n   code or the browser.\n4. Email `support@chainmore.io` to switch the account to live mode.\n5. In live mode: create a `cm_live_` key, add the live payout destination and\n   a live webhook endpoint with its own secret, then run one small real\n   payment.\n";
